{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag","id":1127558,"title":"Vampires and the Stun Tag","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T04:18:37-07:00","id":1127558,"title":"Vampires and the Stun Tag","content":"I hope this is the right place to address this question, but seeing as how my problem is Kindred specific I'll put it here. I know that there has been a fair amount of confusion about how stun is applied as an effect between books in 2nd Edition nWoD going from a doubling of equipment bonus to damage, to a reduction in target successes (by body size) to attain the stun, and back, but I've run into an interesting situation with a game in which I am a player. My character - a confederate sanctified gangrel - is a shootist. He can go claws and savagery, but being a solider he prefers to use the tools and training of a lifetime, and in combat has such skills and training to make shooting someone in the head worthwhile. It's also a useful tactic for aiding other players in group combats if he stuns the target and then others can beat it down.<br /> <br /> This is doubly true in a game with Strix!<br /> <br /> However, the ST has made the claim that vampires can reflexively spend blood to end the stunned tilt regardless of the source. If this were a house rule I would abide it just fine, but he claims this is an official position either from errata or the community at large on 'a forum', but he has neither the time nor inclination to provide me with the bona fides. Does anyone know about this supposed ruling and where I can find it if it even exists? I just want to know so I can draw it up at moment's notice or if it has any permutations for sources of lethal or aggravated damage (like tracer rounds) I have yet to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:12:37-07:00","id":1127572,"title":"","content":"No, vampires can be stunned. They can't undo it by a blood point. However arguments can be made for vampires not being able to be stunned, as a house rule. <br /> All people can end the stunned tilt by spending a willpower point on their turn, but takes a -3 penalty to their action. Reasonably a vampire that heals the damage from the stunning attack, would also loose the tilt. Pepper sprey in the eyes though, that should be healable with a single vitea, though to it being a poison that could be cleansed.<br /> <br /> The strix should probably not be susceptible to stunned , whenever possessing someone(thing) or not. It seems at least to me to go against the never tired, never knocked out creep that are the strix.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, there is no consensus about this on the forum. It is not answered by a dev as far as i know, and it is not in the errata or faq.<br /> <br /> If your ST says something is a rule and doesn't want to show it, your ST is just a douche. If it was a house rule, sure one thing if everyone was on board with that, but calling for a consensus or official rule and not showing it when asked; dick-move.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:18:17-07:00","id":1127616,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not aware of any such rule in an official source. It's not an unreasonable house rule, but as far as I know it is a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:40:32-07:00","id":1127625,"title":"","content":"Vampires can spend blood reflexively to heal damage. If the attendant damage that causes a tilt is healed, the tilt is gone. It's not a house rule. What is ambiguous in the rules is if a tilt requires the attendant damage to be healed &quot;in its entirety&quot;, if &quot;a single point of the damage is healed&quot; or if &quot;just enough damage is healed to put it under the threshold&quot; is sufficient to clear the tilt.<br /> <br /> If your ST has informed you that you aren't going to be able to reliably spam stuns in order to effortlessly murder vampires then it's pretty obvious he is going with the interpretation that a single point of healing is sufficient for a vampire to clear a stun. I wouldn't throw a temper tantrum about it because that means a Strix can't spam their Screech effect to effortlessly kill you either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:40:59-07:00","id":1127626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127572#post1127572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reasonably a vampire that heals the damage from the stunning attack, would also loose the tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunned is the only personal Tilt that doesn't go away when healed. It's actually all the others that specify that they are removed when the damage is healed.<br /> There are some who are capable of removing tilts, but even in those cases they might not be able to do anything about Stunned since removing Tilts generally requires an action (such as Pattern Restoration and Gift activations) and you can't take those actions until Stunned has already passed. Either way vampires have no innate Tilt-removing powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:49:19-07:00","id":1127633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127625#post1127625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is ambiguous in the rules is if a tilt requires the attendant damage to be healed &quot;in its entirety&quot;, if &quot;a single point of the damage is healed&quot; or if &quot;just enough damage is healed to put it under the threshold&quot; is sufficient to clear the tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The VtR core book just says that you need to heal the damage (natural interpretation would still be all the damage dealt in the attack, imo) for the Tilts that can be healed, but Mage actually describes how to bookkeep Tilts and you need to heal all damage inflicted when you got the Tilt. Specifically you need to heal the leftmost box you filled in when you got the Tilt but since you can only heal from right to left it's pretty obvious that you need to heal all damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T09:15:23-07:00","id":1127680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127626#post1127626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stunned is the only personal Tilt that doesn't go away when healed. It's actually all the others that specify that they are removed when the damage is healed.<br /> There are some who are capable of removing tilts, but even in those cases they might not be able to do anything about Stunned since removing Tilts generally requires an action (such as Pattern Restoration and Gift activations) and you can't take those actions until Stunned has already passed. Either way vampires have no innate Tilt-removing powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts or devotions that ignore or &quot;heal&quot; tilts are reflexive, exactly so they aren't useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T10:39:47-07:00","id":1127703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127626#post1127626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stunned is the only personal Tilt that doesn't go away when healed. It's actually all the others that specify that they are removed when the damage is healed.<br /> There are some who are capable of removing tilts, but even in those cases they might not be able to do anything about Stunned since removing Tilts generally requires an action (such as Pattern Restoration and Gift activations) and you can't take those actions until Stunned has already passed. Either way vampires have no innate Tilt-removing powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As i said, reasonable. It's reasonable that the Stunned tilt goes away if the damage that made it heals. But given that the Tilt only lasts for a turn and normal people don't heal damage on a turn it could just be a slight oversight. Pattern restoration isn't a vampires heal ability, because vampires heal reflexively, same but different with werewolves. But yes, by RAW this is missing. However, overall, it doesn't make sense you have a tilt when the damage is gone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T10:45:34-07:00","id":1127706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127680#post1127680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gifts or devotions that ignore or &quot;heal&quot; tilts are reflexive, exactly so they aren't useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially that's house ruling a free Power for all vampires. Question: Which devotion allows healing tilts reflexively? I ask because citing it may help <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3069_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3069\" data-vbnamecard=\"3069\">RuneKnight3</a> demonstrate his point in an open fair dialogue with the ST between games because Devotions are vampire specific example of the rules we are talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-11-2017, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T10:49:46-07:00","id":1127708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127633#post1127633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The VtR core book just says that you need to heal the damage (natural interpretation would still be all the damage dealt in the attack, imo) for the Tilts that can be healed, but Mage actually describes how to bookkeep Tilts and you need to heal all damage inflicted when you got the Tilt. Specifically you need to heal the leftmost box you filled in when you got the Tilt but since you can only heal from right to left it's pretty obvious that you need to heal all damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No this is not correct. The damage from leg-wreck and arm-wreck tilts both goes away when the damage from the attack goes away, not the leftmost damage. The same thing is implied in V:tR 2ed core, however not as clear cut.<br /> <br /> Mage 2ed core p.319-323<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Tilt is inflicted as a result of an attack,<br /> mark an \u2018x\u2019 under the leftmost Health box inflicted in that attack.<br /> The Tilt ends when that damage that caused it has healed </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:19:35-07:00","id":1127739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127708#post1127708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No this is not correct. The damage from leg-wreck and arm-wreck tilts both goes away when the damage from the attack goes away, not the leftmost damage. The same thing is implied in V:tR 2ed core, however not as clear cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't actually disagreeing with Tessie here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127633#post1127633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The VtR core book just says that you need to heal the damage (natural interpretation would still be all the damage dealt in the attack, imo) for the Tilts that can be healed, but Mage actually describes how to bookkeep Tilts and you need to heal all damage inflicted when you got the Tilt. Specifically you need to heal <b>the leftmost box you filled in when you got the Tilt</b> but since you can only heal from right to left it's pretty obvious that you need to heal all damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2ed core p.319-323<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Tilt is inflicted as a result of an attack,<br /> mark an \u2018x\u2019 under <b>the leftmost Health box inflicted in that attack.</b><br /> The Tilt ends when that damage that caused it has healed </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:27:19-07:00","id":1127757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127706#post1127706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially that's house ruling a free Power for all vampires. Question: Which devotion allows healing tilts reflexively? I ask because citing it may help <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> demonstrate his point in an open fair dialogue with the ST between games because Devotions are vampire specific example of the rules we are talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if one is published. Can easily come up with one involving say Resilience and Protean.<br /> <br /> The design space for it in Werewolf is the Purity Facet of the Hunting Wolf Gift, and the Rahu Auspice Blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:29:38-07:00","id":1127758,"title":"","content":"For my games, it depends on where the stunned tilt comes from.<br /> <br /> If the stun tilt comes from physical damage to the kindred, like from a bullet to the skull, then once they heal the damage they are fine.<br /> <br /> If it is from a poison, then hurt locker mentioned that Kindred can flush out toxic substances with a point a vitae.<br /> <br /> If it comes from a devotion/gift/spell then that is where things become slightly more interesting to deal with, and I would make decisions based upon how they were effected by said devotion/gift/spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:30:37-07:00","id":1127760,"title":"","content":"I think it also says something about kindred and tilts when tilts weren't even included in the core rulebook of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:37:22-07:00","id":1127765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127706#post1127706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially that's house ruling a free Power for all vampires. Question: Which devotion allows healing tilts reflexively? I ask because citing it may help <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3069_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3069\" data-vbnamecard=\"3069\">RuneKnight3</a> demonstrate his point in an open fair dialogue with the ST between games because Devotions are vampire specific example of the rules we are talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that VtR 2e doesn't use Tilts. It mentions them once, and refers you back to the CofD core book or the GMC RU. Since it doesn't use Tilts, the book basically never addresses how vampires interact with them. Anything regarding VtR 2e vampires and Tilts is a house rule to start with (at least until the devs get around to addressing vampires and Tilts in an official way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:55:30-07:00","id":1127809,"title":"","content":"The source of my curiosity isn't so much outrage or throwing a tantrum as the presentation of information and the unwillingness or disinterest of the ST to be more transparent when how information was presented inferred that firearms were functionally useless against vampires when that's just not true. There are several reasons to use guns and not just as a Carthian specialist or Bride of Dracula as in nWoD 1st edition. The inclusion of tilts and conditions is a great equalizer and seeing them nerfed - especially to emphasize how awesome a pair of Khaibit PC's in comparison to everyone else - is disheartening. Thankfully that doesn't seem like the case here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:41:59-07:00","id":1127823,"title":"","content":"Guns have the advantage of it being very hard to get large pools of defense against them; another advantage is stuff like incendiary rounds, and shotguns provide 9-again. A large range also helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 08-11-2017, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:20:55-07:00","id":1127839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127760#post1127760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it also says something about kindred and tilts when tilts weren't even included in the core rulebook of 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127765#post1127765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that VtR 2e doesn't use Tilts. It mentions them once, and refers you back to the CofD core book or the GMC RU. Since it doesn't use Tilts, the book basically never addresses how vampires interact with them. Anything regarding VtR 2e vampires and Tilts is a house rule to start with (at least until the devs get around to addressing vampires and Tilts in an official way).</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell are you two talking about? VtR certainly doesn't list that many Tilts compared to CofD or GMCRU, which is a shame, but Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Stunned and Blinded are written out in full in the VtR core book on page 178. How you get them, how they affect you, and how you get rid of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127823#post1127823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guns have the advantage of it being very hard to get large pools of defense against them; another advantage is stuff like incendiary rounds and shotguns provide 9-again. A large range also helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that incendiary rounds do 9 Again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:33:55-07:00","id":1127844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127839#post1127839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell are you two talking about? VtR certainly doesn't list that many Tilts compared to CofD or GMCRU, which is a shame, but Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Stunned and Blinded are written out in full in the VtR core book on page 178. How you get them, how they affect you, and how you get rid of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably because it's been awhile since I read the VtR book, but I really don't remember tilts being in the book. I'll have to check it out, and if it is there, I'm sorry for any misinformation I might've spread. My bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where does it say that incendiary rounds do 9 Again? </div> </div> </div>That would be why commas and grammar are important. I meant that just shot guns were 9-again, and that incendiary rounds existed. I'll change that after I post this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:37:25-07:00","id":1127847,"title":"","content":"Yup, checked it and Tessie's right about tilts being in there. Sorry for any misinformation on it not being in the book, folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:09:26-07:00","id":1127866,"title":"","content":"Huh. I remember 2e not having Tilts in it too. This is some Berenstain Bears shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:52:09-07:00","id":1127881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127844#post1127844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably because it's been awhile since I read the VtR book, but I really don't remember tilts being in the book. I'll have to check it out, and if it is there, I'm sorry for any misinformation I might've spread. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay. I was just baffled that two people in a row claimed Tilts didn't exist in VtR when I just had read up on Tilts in VtR to write an earlier post in this thread (where I actually mentioned what VtR says about healing them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127866#post1127866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I remember 2e not having Tilts in it too. This is some Berenstain Bears shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it's baked into Specified Targets. There's no appendix or even separate heading for Tilts. Not even subheadings for the individual Tilts.<br /> (Also, C-3PO had a silver leg in the original trilogy.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127844#post1127844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be why commas and grammar are important. I meant that just shot guns were 9-again, and that incendiary rounds existed. I'll change that after I post this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, are there any special rules for incendiary rounds for vampires? My reading of the core book suggests incendiary ammunition wouldn't be any different from regular ammunition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:37:26-07:00","id":1127888,"title":"","content":"In the old Armory book, Dragonsbreath rounds and Flares actually create fires with attendant rules regarding flame size and intensity. Tracer rounds had a slim chance of igniting combustible materials. Very unlikely to burn a vampire but if they're wearing flammable clothes from the 1700s or doused with gasoline they could be ignited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:52:35-07:00","id":1127892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127881#post1127881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, are there any special rules for incendiary rounds for vampires? My reading of the core book suggests incendiary ammunition wouldn't be any different from regular ammunition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just generally rule incendiary rounds as doing lethal damage to vampires, but I'll have to check Hurt Locker for any specific rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:58:13-07:00","id":1127894,"title":"","content":"... Um, I said directly that VtR 2e addresses Tilts. What I said is that VtR 2e doesn't <b>use</b> the Tilt system like the other games do. As you noted, it just has some of them as status effects for specified targets. The rest of the 2e supernaturals have powers (either innate or bought) that interact with Tilts; either inflicting them, protecting you from them, or removing them. That's why anything that imports the full Tilt system to VtR 2e is inherently a house rule. It's not designed to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:57:23-07:00","id":1127991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127558-vampires-and-the-stun-tag?p=1127739#post1127739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't actually disagreeing with Tessie here.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, misread it then. Thanks for pointing it out. Sorry Tessie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.t